{"parentUuid":"26153e70-f75b-4ad1-8013-c9cf83a6cc2d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"1dec08eb-1192-430c-a9b6-908b7c1cfee7","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"graceful-roaming-otter","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_vrtx_01FL3SaovDrvyFqF5dKMxUGG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the sample data and my knowledge of the Google cluster data schema:\n\n**Task events (13 columns):**\n1. timestamp (microseconds)\n2. missing info\n3. job ID\n4. task index\n5. machine ID\n6. event type (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING)\n7. user\n8. scheduling class\n9. priority\n10. CPU request\n11. memory request\n12. disk space request\n13. different machines constraint\n\n**Job events (8 columns):**\n1. timestamp (microseconds)\n2. missing info\n3. job ID\n4. event type (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING)\n5. user\n6. scheduling class\n7. job name\n8. logical job name\n\nLet me create the datatypes directory and implement the TaskEvent and JobEvent classes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":49450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":222,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXXogwJhCJqyJhc7teWSs","type":"assistant","uuid":"12f8908b-d491-47a0-b129-df17b0055c85","timestamp":"2026-01-27T11:29:54.563Z"}
